    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>I want to plot a graph with all the dates in x axis.</div><div>Here is the code I used</div><div><br></div><div>```</div><div>library(tidyverse)</div><div>library(readxl)</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>data &lt;- readxl::read_excel(&quot;Sentinel-1 Metadata info.xls&quot;)</div><div>centroid &lt;- slice(data,1)</div><div><br></div><div>data %&gt;% </div><div>  ggplot(aes(`Date of acquisition`, `Bperp(m)`)) +</div><div>  geom_point() +</div><div>  geom_segment(aes(x = centroid$`Date of acquisition`, y = centroid$`Bperp(m)`, </div><div>                   xend = `Date of acquisition`, yend = `Bperp(m)`)) +</div><div>  theme_minimal()</div><div>```</div><div>I got the graph like this</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2/attach/43145ab93e9a/Screenshot%20from%202020-04-09%2012-29-38.png?part=0.1&amp;view=1\" alt=\"Screenshot from 2020-04-09 12-29-38.png\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" width=\"320\" height=\"198\"></p><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>But I want to display all the dates in the format DDMMYYYY.</div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div>"
