   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif\">Two things,</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif\">you should not pass values to arguments within `aes`. For example, you do</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif\">aes(x = centroid$`Date of acquisition`...)<br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif\">but should be</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif\">aes(x = `Date of acquisition`...)</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif\">The error message says that your variable is (Date of acquisition) is not in the proper Date format. You will have to use `as.Date` to properly convert what you have now to a Date format. If help file for as.Date is not clear enough, please search the internet. This question has been answered many times.</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif\">Cheers,</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif\">Roman </div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif\"><br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
